sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Worker@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP audio validation worker
    participant Validators@{ "type": "entity" } as opusinfo + opusdec<br/>inside this worker
    participant API@{ "type": "control" } as Dictaphone API
    participant FileStore@{ "type": "database" } as File-linked object storage

    Worker->>API: GET /audio-jobs/validation/next<br/>Authorization: Bearer worker token
    alt No job available
        API-->>Worker: 204 No Content
    else Validation job available
        API-->>Worker: Job id, job_kind, signed source_url
        Worker->>Worker: Create temporary job directory under work_dir
        Worker->>FileStore: GET source_url
        Worker->>Validators: Run opusinfo, then<br/>opusdec --quiet source /dev/null

        alt Download or validation fails
            Worker->>Worker: Build failure completion with error message
            Worker->>API: POST /audio-jobs/validation/complete<br/>Bearer token<br/>id and status=failure with error
        else Validation succeeds
            Validators-->>Worker: Audio stream validated
            Worker->>API: POST /audio-jobs/validation/complete<br/>Bearer token<br/>id and status=success
        end
    end
    Worker->>Worker: Clean work_dir in finally block

    Note over Worker,API: The worker polls once, processes at most one job, reports to the fixed completion endpoint, and exits.
    Note over Worker,Validators: Both validation commands run inside this worker's isolated environment.
